;; TENSION LEDGER v1 -- the carrier proposed by DESIGN-tensions-as-patterns.md:86
;; (section 3), implemented by worklist row :U41.
;;
;; WHAT THIS IS.  Three prose tensions live in a mission doc's **Carried
;; tensions** sentence (futon2/holes/missions/M-zaif-harness-v1.md:35-39) and are
;; already referenced BY NUMBER as premises by other rows.  This file is the same
;; three, typed, so that "what is the machine carrying, and what has it learned"
;; is a query rather than a grep chain.
;;
;; WHAT THIS IS NOT.  Not a ruling surface.  Rulings live in aif-equations.edn
;; :choices and control-map-edges.edn :decisions, and Joe writes them.  A status
;; here is a SCORE with pointers, and no status moved in the retrofit: all three
;; seeds are :carried, which is what their evidence says today.  Nothing reads
;; this file on the live path -- no tick, no selector, no weight (the U39 learning
;; -feed containment, runs/U39-selection-retrospective/README.md:317-330, applies
;; to this ledger too).
;;
;; APPEND-ONLY.  Tension records are never edited in place.  :tension/status is
;; the status AT MINT and equals the type of that tension's mint event; the
;; CURRENT status is the fold of :events (u41_tension_ledger.bb computes it and
;; the validator refuses a record whose field claims otherwise).  That reading is
;; a design judgement of this row, taken because it is the one that keeps section
;; 3's field name AND its "never edits in place" discipline at the same time --
;; and because U39's mint edge (README.md:265-288) writes :tension/status :carried
;; at mint, so the mint record shape is consumed here unforked.
{:ledger/id :wm-contract/tension-ledger
 :ledger/version "v1"
 :ledger/row :U41
 :ledger/written-by "claude-1, wm-edge lane, 2026-09-03"
 :ledger/implements "DESIGN-tensions-as-patterns.md:86-101 (section 3)"
